    -- pre-gate-3 name-path rename, which retires the old row, gives the collection a new id and renames the chunks first; the cascade
    -- renames each child by name and the id repair follows. Step 1 missed (the chunk now carries the new id), and step 2 would scan the
    -- tenant's leaf once per cascaded row, N x N. One probe on the registry's (tenant_id, collection_id) key skips it.
